# UnrealMCP Data + Sequencer Domains — 2026-07-03

Status: implementation complete; verification state recorded below.
Scope rule honored: no Niagara files touched (parallel Niagara workflow active; its editor cycles also hold the plugin DLL, so builds must be timed between cycles).

## What was added

### DataTable / DataAsset domain (`data`, 9 tools)

- C++: `Commands/UnrealMCPDataCommands.{h,cpp}` — schema read, row list/get/add-or-update/remove, DataTable create (row struct by path), DataAsset read/property-set/create. Rows and properties round-trip through `FJsonObjectConverter` against the row struct / class, so payloads are plain JSON keyed by field name.
- Python: `tools/data_tools.py`. Docs: `Docs/Tools/data_tools.md`.
- Guards: MCP-dependency rejection on creation paths and value payloads; abstract `UDataAsset` classes are rejected before asset creation; mutations wrapped in one `FScopedTransaction` via the shared `IsReadOnlyCommandName` dispatch wrapper; `save=True` default with explicit `saved` readback.

### Sequencer domain (`sequencer`, 5 tools)

- C++: `Commands/UnrealMCPSequencerCommands.{h,cpp}` — create Level Sequence (display rate + playback range), info readback (bindings/tracks/camera-cut presence), possessable actor binding by label, transform-track cubic keyframes (double channels 0-8), camera cut sections.
- Python: `tools/sequencer_tools.py`. Docs: `Docs/Tools/sequencer_tools.md` (includes the shot-blocking flow).
- First-pass limitations recorded in the tool doc: possessables only, single transform section, cubic keys only, no property/audio/subsequence tracks.
- Build.cs additions: `LevelSequence`, `MovieScene`, `MovieSceneTracks`.

### A-pass (same day)

- Null-guard sweep (non-Niagara): the only remaining unguarded `GEditor` dereference (`UnrealMCPBlueprintCommands.cpp` spawn path) was fixed; `FindFProperty` sites (28) and same-line `Cast<>()->` patterns scanned clean — the original audit overstated these.
- `Docs/Tools/pcg_tools.md` fully resynced to the 21 registered PCG tools (was ~40% coverage, with several stale entries).

## Registration / gates

- Total registered tools after the Landscape foliage-removal extension: 328 (`data` 9, `sequencer` 10, `skeletal` 6, `landscape` 7); registration-smoke minimums updated (`data` >= 8, `sequencer` >= 9, `skeletal` >= 5, `landscape` >= 6).
- Offline gates green at authoring time: py_compile, server import, ruff F821, registration smoke.

